oh-my-jeo
=========

oh-my-jeo is a derivative work of oh-my-hermes.

Upstream project : oh-my-hermes
Upstream author  : @rlaope and the oh-my-hermes contributors
Upstream source  : https://github.com/rlaope/oh-my-hermes
Upstream commit  : 117f67a2347b82ea527ca1d7f8c0e8d609ec8c4c (v3.0.2, 2026-10-11)
Upstream license : MIT License (see LICENSE)

The oh-my-hermes 1.0.1 engine and skill catalog are inherited under the terms
of the MIT License. Selected oh-my-hermes v3.0.2 adaptations (routing,
plugin interface, intent classification) are also adopted. The original
copyright notice is retained in LICENSE. Full upstream runtime parity is not
claimed; only documented adoptions listed below are in place.

Changes made in oh-my-jeo:
  - oh-my-jeo brand identity, README, and architecture/workflow visualization
  - Generated oh-my-jeo icon (assets/oh-my-jeo-icon.png, 1024×1024 PNG) and
    provenance metadata (assets/oh-my-jeo-icon.json). Generated by GPT-6.1-sol
    on 2026-10-12 under the same MIT license terms. Converted and processed for
    deployment using Python standard-library and native macOS tools. Not an
    execution or verification claim.
  - oh-my-jeo agent specification (docs/OH_MY_JEO_AGENT_SPEC.md) describing an
    independent coding-agent profile layered on the inherited contract engine.
  - Selected v3.0.2 adaptations: routing interface updates, plugin architecture
    refinements, intent classification improvements, Latin recall, EN/FR
    relative-time/French review cues, retained callback lifecycle, and catalog
    planning/test/review/debug/forensics/backend guidance adopted from upstream.

The Python package import namespace and CLI entry point (`omj`) are retained
from upstream for binary/skill-catalog compatibility; the `omj` brand is layered
on top. See README.md ("Origin & attribution") for details.
